-- title:
--   Cascade Zeta1 Bound General
-- statement:
--   **The general first-stage cascade bound has the same explicit envelope form.**
--
--   Assume the cascade hypotheses, the coarse bound on `nu`, and exclude the exceptional branch $k=1$ and $m=1$. Then
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{cascadeZeta1}(\mathrm{params},\varepsilon,\operatorname{cascadeSigma}(\mathrm{params},k,\nu))
--   \le20204\,k^2m^4\,\operatorname{stepEnvelope}(\mathrm{params},k,\varepsilon,2048,160000).
--   $$
--
--   The theorem combines the tight first-stage estimate with the degree-size and square-root envelope bounds. Together with the exceptional branch it yields a uniform first-stage estimate.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Test.cascadeZeta1_bound_general`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Test/MainTheorem/ScalarBounds/CascadeBounds/SigmaZeta1.lean#L237-L401

